H: Men die earlier than women adn have higher mortality chances at every age from heart attack.
T: Cardiac Health
C: USA
D: 1948-2023
O: Framingham Heart Study
B: The study analysing a sample of 15k americans over 75years found that average age for male death was 65 while female age was 70, for heart diseases. While there are more female deaths than male, the age group of 35-64 have 92k male deaths every year, twice that of the female counterpart. Even when optimising for serum lipids, total blood pressure, cholestrol, smoking status, diabetes, BMI and physical activities, men posses 2x higher chnaces of heart attack than women, indicating the reasons are primarily not rooted in "lifestyle choices".
U: https://www.framinghamheartstudy.org/
